# Orchestration

You are the parent. You orchestrate, manage, review, and merge if required. You do not implement work you have handed to a child.

- Spawn luna (Codex `gpt-5.6-luna`) or agy (`gemini-3.7-flash --effort high`) for implementation and research. Follow the `spawn-child-agents` skill.
- After spawn, set wait timers (`AwaitShell`) until the child exits. Do not leave the user to wake you.
- Children commit themselves when their tests pass. Do not wait for the user to tell them to commit. Do not push unless the user asked.
- After a child finishes: review the diff/commit, fix or send them back if needed, merge only when required (conflicts, stacked branches, integrating sequential work).
- Prepare handoffs as files. Run children in parallel only when they cannot interfere (no overlapping files, no shared commits on the same branch). Otherwise run them sequentially.
